WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.936
-President Trump declared
a national emergency on Friday,

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:05.538
and then spent
the rest of the weekend

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.606
lashing out at critics.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.107
For more on this,
it's time for

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:09.609
"A Closer Look."

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:13.312
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:15.881
After Trump unilaterally
bypassed Congress

00:00:15.881 --> 00:00:17.850
by declaring
a fake national emergency

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.719
to build his border wall,
he spent the rest of the weekend

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:22.054
calling the media
the enemy of the people,

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:24.257
demanded retribution
against TV networks,

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:25.792
and called
Justice Department officials

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.560
who investigated him treasonous.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.696
It's more obvious every day
that Trump's natural inclination

00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:31.998
is to be a dictator.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:34.300
He could even try to grow
a dictator mustache,

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.235
but based on the rest
of his hair situation,

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:37.570
I'm not sure.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.438
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:41.941
And Trump would be even scarier

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.476
if he weren't
so easily distracted.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:45.812
For example, he couldn't
even make it 24 hours

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.713
after declaring
his national emergency

00:00:47.713 --> 00:00:50.049
before he escaped to Florida
for a weekend of golf

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:53.152
and lounging around at
his private club in Palm Beach,

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:55.921
where he was spotted on Saturday
waiting for breakfast.

00:00:55.921 --> 00:00:57.623
-President Trump
spending his first day

00:00:57.623 --> 00:00:59.425
following
that emergency declaration

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.961
at the Trump International
Golf Club down in Palm Beach,

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:04.197
and this photo
of President Trump

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:06.632
at the club's omelette bar
went viral,

00:01:06.632 --> 00:01:09.636
getting retweeted
thousands of times over.

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:12.438
-There's no clearer sign
this is not a real emergency

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:15.474
than the fact that
he is at an omelette bar.

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:19.378
In real emergency,
no one goes to the omelette bar.

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:20.746
"The building is on fire!"

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:22.014
[ As Donald Trump ] "I'll be
right there! Oh, yeah!

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:25.118
Onions, green peppers, ham --
Do you have ham?"

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.086
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.321
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:29.321 --> 00:01:32.158
"Put it in a to-go box!"

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.594
[ Normal voice ] Also, it's good
to see your emergency wear is

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:37.730
the official uniform
of golf grandpas everywhere.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.031
Look at him.

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:42.035
He looks like
a 6-foot-tall Band-Aid.

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:43.936
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:45.838
I'm shocked that he wasn't
wearing a fanny pack

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:49.342
and trying to get them
to take an expired coupon.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:52.278
I'm sorry, but that is not how
a president should look ever,

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.814
but especially
during an emergency.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.348
When President Obama
got Bin Laden,

00:01:56.348 --> 00:01:58.484
he was in the situation room
surrounded by generals.

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:00.687
Can you imagine Trump
overseeing that mission

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:04.723
from the omelette bar
at his golf club?

00:02:04.723 --> 00:02:06.826
[ As Donald Trump ] Navy SEALs,
this is your president.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:09.228
Give me full situ-- Wait.
Hold on. What's that?

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.064
Yeah, yeah, hash browns."

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.066
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:15.067
[ Normal voice ] And even when
he's not in Florida golfing

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.502
and eating soft foods,

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:18.771
it's clear we've elected
as our president

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:21.640
an adult grandpa who has trouble
forming coherent sentences.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.909
For example, during his
press conference on Friday,

00:02:23.909 --> 00:02:26.912
Trump explained that he expected
a protracted court challenge

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:28.614
to his national emergency
declaration,

00:02:28.614 --> 00:02:30.883
although it was less
of an explanation

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:33.253
and more of a sing-song ramble.

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:34.854
-I'll sign the final papers

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:38.657
as soon as I get
into the Oval Office.

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:41.126
And we will have
a national emergency.

00:02:41.126 --> 00:02:42.695
And we will then be sued.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:45.364
And they will sue us
in the ninth circuit,

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:47.666
even though
it shouldn't be there.

00:02:47.666 --> 00:02:50.336
And we will possibly
get a bad ruling.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.605
And then we'll get
another bad ruling.

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.807
And then we'll end up
in the Supreme Court.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.843
And, hopefully,
we'll get a fair shake.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.811
And we'll win
in the Supreme Court,

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.013
just like the ban.

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:02.749
They sued us
in the ninth circuit,

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:03.849
and we lost.

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:06.252
And then we lost
in the appellate division.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.254
And there we went
to the Supreme Court,

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.689
and we won.

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.691
-he sounds like a 5-year-old

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:14.227
telling you
what he saw at the zoo.

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:16.896
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:20.533
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.568
[ As Donald Trump ]
"And then we saw the monkeys,

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:24.737
and they were eating bananas,

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.706
and Todd said,
'We used to be apes,'

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.274
and I said that's not true,

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.776
and Todd said, 'Yes, it is!',

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:33.546
and then a bird
crapped on his head.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.814
[ Normal voice ] Of course,
it's true that Trump's

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.816
national emergency declaration

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.017
will be challenged in court,

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:40.018
given that it's very likely
unconstitutional.

00:03:40.018 --> 00:03:42.722
If Trump has any chance
of winning in court, at all,

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.458
He has to insist that
this was his only choice,

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:48.294
that he had one thing,
one thing he had to say.

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:51.597
This is a real emergency.
We had to do it this way.

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:53.599
-I could do the wall
over a longer period of time.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:55.601
I didn't need to do this.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:57.537
But I'd rather do it
much faster.

00:03:57.537 --> 00:04:00.706
-You didn't need to do this --
then it's not an emergency.

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:02.475
That's the exact opposite
of an emergency.

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:03.776
That's a choice.

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:06.278
That's like saying,
"I'm having emergency surgery

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:08.114
to get butt implants."

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:10.182
[ Laughter ]
"I didn't need to do this,

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:12.751
but I hate doing squats."

00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:15.521
When he heard that,
even Rudy Giuliani said,

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.690
"Oh, no.
You shouldn't have said that."

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.792
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:22.361
Trump might even know
on some level

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:24.363
that his national emergency
stands no chance

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:25.765
of surviving a court challenge,

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.266
and he very likely doesn't care,

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:29.368
because he's doing this entirely

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:32.171
to please a very narrow set
of right wing pundits

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:33.906
who hectored him
into building the wall,

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:36.208
like Rush Limbaugh,
who Trump actually namechecked

00:04:36.208 --> 00:04:38.077
during his press conference
on Friday.

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:40.179
-Mr. President, could you
tell us to what degree

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.581
some of the outside
conservative voices

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:44.016
helped to shape your views

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:46.452
on this national emergency?
-I would talk about it.

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:50.757
Look, Sean Hannity has been
a terrific, terrific,

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:52.691
uh, supporter of what I do.

00:04:52.691 --> 00:04:54.059
Not of me.

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:56.095
If I changed my views,
he wouldn't be with me.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:59.298
Rush Limbaugh,
I think he's a great guy.

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:02.034
He can speak for three hours
without a phone call.

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:05.271
Try doing that sometime.
For three hours, he speaks.

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:06.873
He's got one of
the biggest audiences

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:07.940
in the history of the world.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.808
I mean,
this guy is unbelievable.

00:05:09.808 --> 00:05:12.644
Try speaking for three hours
without taking calls.

00:05:12.644 --> 00:05:13.946
Taking calls is easy.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:16.682
Okay, I'll answer this one,
I'll answer that one.

00:05:16.682 --> 00:05:18.584
He goes for three hours,

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.919
and he's got an audience
that's fantastic.

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:23.556
-My God, that answer
took three hours.

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:25.024
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.659
Also, if he's talking for three
hours without taking calls,

00:05:27.659 --> 00:05:30.363
maybe nobody is calling him.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:33.032
[ As Rush Limbaugh ]
We're gonna open the phone line!

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:37.069
[ Applause ]

00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:39.772
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.507
And even if you
put aside the chaos

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:43.909
this is causing here at home,
it definitely seems like

00:05:43.909 --> 00:05:45.978
all of this is hurting our image
around the world, too.

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.113
Vice President Mike Pence
discovered that over the weekend

00:05:48.113 --> 00:05:49.315
when he mentioned
President Trump

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:50.516
in his speech in Munich.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:53.619
He clearly thought it was
gonna be an applause line

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:55.521
and it definitely was not.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:57.690
-I bring greetings
from the 45th president

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.859
of the United States of America,

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:02.528
President Donald Trump.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:05.965
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:07.767
Last August...

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.302
-Say what you want
about Mike Pence,

00:06:10.302 --> 00:06:13.306
the man knows how
to hold for silence.

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:14.773
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.773 --> 00:06:16.942
Never thought I would say this,
but Pence might have

00:06:16.942 --> 00:06:19.345
to hire Jeb Bush
as his hype man.

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:21.814
-I bring greetings
from the 45th President

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:23.916
of the United States of America,

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:27.419
President Donald Trump.

00:06:27.419 --> 00:06:28.754
-Please clap.

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:30.656
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:34.459
-But a reaction like that...
[ Applause ]

00:06:34.459 --> 00:06:37.029
A reaction like that must
really sting for Trump,

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:38.564
who craves validation
and praise.

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:40.733
In fact, over the weekend,
we learned that Trump asked

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.034
the prime minister of Japan

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:44.036
to nominate him
for a Nobel Prize.

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:45.905
A Japanese newspaper reported

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:48.874
that Japanese Prime Minister
Shinzo Abe nominated Trump

00:06:48.874 --> 00:06:50.876
for the Nobel Peace Prize
last autumn

00:06:50.876 --> 00:06:54.012
after receiving a request from
the U.S. government to do so,

00:06:54.012 --> 00:06:55.614
which is especially
embarrassing,

00:06:55.614 --> 00:06:58.116
given that on Friday,
Trump bragged about the fact

00:06:58.116 --> 00:07:00.285
that Abe had nominated him
for the Nobel Prize

00:07:00.285 --> 00:07:03.656
and claimed he had no idea
he was about to do that.

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:06.192
-Prime Minister Abe of Japan

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:10.762
gave me the most beautiful
copy of a letter

00:07:10.762 --> 00:07:13.532
that he sent to the people

00:07:13.532 --> 00:07:15.767
who give out a thing
called the Nobel Prize.

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:18.270
He said, "I have nominated you,

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:22.307
or respectfully,
on behalf of Japan,

00:07:22.307 --> 00:07:25.577
I am asking them to give you
the Nobel Peace Prize."

00:07:25.577 --> 00:07:27.213
I said, "Thank you."

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:29.414
-Oh, really?
You said thank you?

00:07:29.414 --> 00:07:31.517
Did you also bribe him?
"Here you go, Shinzo.

00:07:31.517 --> 00:07:33.886
This is for one free omelette.

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:35.754
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.754 --> 00:07:38.824
It is expired.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:38.824 --> 00:07:41.127
So, maybe just frame it."

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:44.197
Somehow I doubt that Trump will
get that Nobel Peace Prize

00:07:44.197 --> 00:07:45.764
after unilaterally declaring

00:07:45.764 --> 00:07:48.233
a nonexistent emergency
at our border with Mexico.

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:49.935
For weeks,
Trump has gone back and forth

00:07:49.935 --> 00:07:51.604
on the possibility
of declaring an emergency,

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:54.140
while also insisting he was
already building the wall,

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:56.809
as he did right before
the State of the Union address,

00:07:56.809 --> 00:07:58.977
although he was
very coy about it.

00:07:58.977 --> 00:08:01.447
-Are you saying now you expect
to declare a national --

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:03.048
-I don't want to say,
but you'll hear

00:08:03.048 --> 00:08:05.384
the State of the Union,
and then you'll see

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:07.653
what happens right after
the State of the Union, okay?

00:08:07.653 --> 00:08:09.255
-You'll hear
the State of the Union,

00:08:09.255 --> 00:08:11.957
And then you'll see what happens
after the State of the Union.

00:08:11.957 --> 00:08:13.825
Trump is so out of his depth,

00:08:13.825 --> 00:08:17.162
he's dodging questions
by explaining how time works.

00:08:17.162 --> 00:08:18.997
[ Laughter ]
"Mr. President,

00:08:18.997 --> 00:08:20.900
didn't you say Mexico
would pay for the wall?

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.935
[ As Donald Trump ] I said
Mexico will pay for the wall

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:24.403
in the future,
not the present.

00:08:24.403 --> 00:08:27.005
And everyone knows the future
comes after the present,

00:08:27.005 --> 00:08:30.075
as opposed to the past,
which is before the present.

00:08:30.075 --> 00:08:31.510
And we can't go
back to the past.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.612
We can only go
back to the future,

00:08:33.612 --> 00:08:35.013
which I learned
from that documentary

00:08:35.013 --> 00:08:36.415
about Bernie Sanders.

00:08:36.415 --> 00:08:39.685
[ Laughter ]

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:42.254
[ Cheers and applause ]
The reason...

00:08:42.254 --> 00:08:43.923
The reason Trump
spent so many weeks

00:08:43.923 --> 00:08:45.324
seesawing back and forth is

00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:46.725
because Republicans
were reportedly

00:08:46.725 --> 00:08:49.028
urging him not to declare
the national emergency,

00:08:49.028 --> 00:08:52.198
knowing the move would be
unpopular and unconstitutional,

00:08:52.198 --> 00:08:54.367
and yet as soon as Trump did it,

00:08:54.367 --> 00:08:55.901
Republicans either supported him

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:57.636
or were muted
in their criticism,

00:08:57.636 --> 00:08:59.238
like Iowa Senator
Chuck Grassley,

00:08:59.238 --> 00:09:01.406
who only said, "I wish
he wouldn't have done it."

00:09:01.406 --> 00:09:04.309
But Grassley was much angrier
when GOP Senate majority Leader

00:09:04.309 --> 00:09:06.112
Mitch McConnell took
to the Senate floor last week

00:09:06.112 --> 00:09:08.180
to announce that Trump would
declare a national emergency.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:11.150
Grassley was talking about
something totally unrelated

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.219
and got mad when McConnell
interrupted him.

00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:18.257
-Allowing these tax credits
incentives to lapse

00:09:18.257 --> 00:09:21.894
has created uncertainty
for investors,

00:09:21.894 --> 00:09:24.096
and the industry
about the availability

00:09:24.096 --> 00:09:25.430
of these credits...
-Will the Senator yield?

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:28.634
-...jeopardizing
the long-term investments

00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:32.671
necessary for the development
of these biofuels.

00:09:32.671 --> 00:09:34.473
I hope the next time

00:09:34.473 --> 00:09:36.141
I get a chance
to have the floor,

00:09:36.141 --> 00:09:37.410
I won't be interrupted.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:39.311
I yield the floor and put
the rest of my statement

00:09:39.311 --> 00:09:41.980
in the record.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:43.916
-Mr. President?
-Leader McConnell.

00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:45.918
-You know you're old
when the young one

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:48.654
disrespecting you
is Mitch McConnell.

00:09:48.654 --> 00:09:50.689
[ Laughter ]

00:09:50.689 --> 00:09:52.191
That's how loud Grassley yells

00:09:52.191 --> 00:09:55.027
when Trump cuts him in line
at the omelette bar.

00:09:55.027 --> 00:09:56.562
[ Laughter ]

00:09:58.764 --> 00:10:00.098
[ Laughter ]

00:10:00.098 --> 00:10:01.600
We're at the whims
of angry old men

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:02.768
screaming about stuff they hear

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:04.436
on talk radio
or see on Fox News.

00:10:04.436 --> 00:10:07.006
Trump just rambles aimlessly
from one topic to the next,

00:10:07.006 --> 00:10:09.108
and his alternate reality
is reinforced

00:10:09.108 --> 00:10:11.009
by the right wing pundits,
who support him.

00:10:11.009 --> 00:10:13.012
Trump is obviously
unfit to be president.

00:10:13.012 --> 00:10:14.646
And if someone
beats him in 2020,

00:10:14.646 --> 00:10:15.815
that person's going to get...

00:10:15.815 --> 00:10:18.017
-A thing called the Nobel Prize.

00:10:18.017 --> 00:10:20.019
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:10:20.019 --> 00:10:21.587
[ Cheers and applause ]

